# Per-project development domains, so each project gets its own cookie jar.
#
# Nothing is edited here by hand. One file per domain lives in sites/, and `lokl` writes
# them alongside the /etc/hosts entry each domain needs in order to resolve at all:
#
#   lokl add my-custom-project
#   lokl port my-custom-project
#   lokl list
#   lokl remove my-custom-project
#
# Two things about this file are load-bearing:
#
#   import  Caddy resolves an import path against the directory of the file holding it,
#           and does not follow this file's symlink back to the repo, so the playbook
#           links <caddy etc>/sites at the repo's sites/ as well. A glob matching nothing
#           is a warning rather than an error, so an empty sites/ still starts.
#   http:// Every generated site block carries the scheme. Without it Caddy treats the
#           site as HTTPS, issues a certificate from its internal CA and asks to be
#           trusted, which nothing on loopback gains anything from.

# Covers a site added by hand without the http:// prefix, which would otherwise still
# reach for a certificate. The comment is not decoration: `caddy fmt` treats a comment as
# attached to whatever follows it and collapses the blank line between the two, so
# without one here every reload warns that the file is unformatted.
{
	auto_https off
}

import sites/*.caddyfile
